-- title:
--   Existence of level automorphisms at q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) be the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which is assumed equal to the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image, under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$. The assertion is that for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$ there exists an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) for the data $(L, q, \zeta, q, q^2M', H, \gamma^{-1})$: that is, for every weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ (as a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$), all integral power series $p_f, p_g$ whose images in $\mathbb{C}[[X]]$ are the $q$-expansions of $f$ and $g$ at width $1$, with the Laurent series attached to $p_g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ nonzero, every $x \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the ratio of those attached to $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of $\tau(x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \gamma^{\sharp}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \gamma^{\sharp}$, where $\gamma^{\sharp} =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.conjElemN q γ⁻¹`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L13) is the real matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/q \\ qc & d\end{pmatrix}$ for $\gamma^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   This is the existence, in the case $q = 2$, of the level automorphism of the base-changed $q$-expansion field of $X_H(q^2M')$ attached to an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$, in the classical sense of the action of the adelic/diagonal conjugation $\mathrm{diag}(q,1)^{-1}\gamma\,\mathrm{diag}(q,1)$ on $q$-expansions. It is used in the analysis of the fibre over the Gauss–$\Gamma_0$ composite, where it feeds the statement that the relevant prime has ramification index one and separable residue extension.
